Senior DevOps / Cloud Engineer – 5 to 8 Years Experience

Senior DevOps / Cloud Engineer 

If you’re aiming for senior roles, these are the expectations interviewers have from 5–8 yrs professionals 👇

🔹 Architecture & Design
• How do you design a highly available and fault-tolerant system on AWS?
• How do you choose between ECS, EKS, and Lambda for production workloads?
• How do you handle multi-region architecture and DR strategy?

🔹 CI/CD & Automation
• How do you design scalable CI/CD pipelines for microservices?
• How do you manage secrets securely in CI/CD?
• How do you implement zero-downtime deployments?
• How do you handle rollback strategies in production?

🔹 Docker & Kubernetes
• How do you optimize Docker images for production?
• How do you troubleshoot Kubernetes pod crash loops?
• How do you design Kubernetes for high availability?
• How do you manage cluster upgrades with minimal downtime?
🔹 Infrastructure as Code
• How do you manage large Terraform codebases?
• How do you handle Terraform state and locking in teams?
• How do you manage multi-account AWS using Terraform?

🔹 Monitoring, Logging & Reliability
• How do you define SLIs, SLOs, and SLAs?
• How do you design monitoring for microservices?
• How do you handle alert fatigue?
• How do you debug production incidents?

🔹 Security & Cost Optimization
• How do you implement DevSecOps in pipelines?
• How do you manage IAM at scale?
• How do you optimize cloud cost without impacting performance?

🔹 Leadership & Ownership
• How do you mentor junior DevOps engineers?
• How do you handle production outages as a lead?
• How do you communicate risks to stakeholders?

💡 Senior roles are not about tools — they’re about decisions, ownership, and impact.
